) VALUES (
  'inflation-rises-to-5-2-percent-october-fuel-2026-11-18',
  'Inflation climbs to 5.2% in October as fuel costs push prices up',
  'Business', '2026-11-18', 'Cape Town Etc', 'https://www.capetownetc.com/news/south-africa-inflation-rises-to-5-2-as-food-and-fuel-prices-climb/',
  'Annual consumer inflation reached 5.2% in October, up from 4.5% in September, with fuel and transport the biggest drivers, according to Stats SA data.',
  'Stats SA data shows the yearly inflation rate reached 5.2% for October, compared with 4.5% the month before. Prices rose 0.7% from September to October, and the annual rate is the highest since May 2024.

Transport was the main driver. Transport inflation reached 15.2% and added 2.1 percentage points to the headline rate. Fuel was up 11.8% over the month and 42.9% over the year, and BusinessDay reports that petrol went above R30 a litre for the first time in October. Core inflation, which leaves out food and fuel, edged up to 4.2% from 4%.

Food prices were mixed. Vegetables rose 8.1% over the year, with onions up 53.6% and potatoes up 14.9%, while meat inflation eased to 0.2%. Cereals continued to fall, with maize meal down 9.0%.

The figures matter to households and to interest rates: BusinessDay says the Reserve Bank''s Monetary Policy Committee was due to announce its next decision, with the repo rate currently at 7.25%. Analysts quoted there are split between a 25-basis-point increase and a pause.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.capetownetc.com/news/south-africa-inflation-rises-to-5-2-as-food-and-fuel-prices-climb/", "https://www.businessday.co.za/economy/2026-11-19-october-inflation-spike-backs-case-for-rate-hike/"]',
  'agent'
);
